# R3F runtime layer

`components/` renders and drives the scene. `hooks/` bridges pure `systems/` logic to
the R3F runtime. `ui/` is DOM overlay outside the Canvas.

## Per-frame work

- Anything that runs every frame belongs in `useFrame`, not `useEffect` and not a
  `setInterval`. `useEffect` is for subscriptions and one-shot setup only.
- Prefer the real `delta` from `useFrame` over `Date.now()`. `Scene.tsx` clamps it to 100 ms before
  passing it to the AI so a backgrounded tab cannot teleport players; keep that clamp.
- Do not allocate inside `useFrame`. Hoist `THREE.Vector3`/`Quaternion` scratch objects
  to module scope or a ref and reuse them. Memoize geometries and materials with `useMemo`.
- Never call `set*` on the Zustand store every frame for values only the renderer needs;
  write to a ref and publish to the store only when other systems must observe it.

## Physics

- Rapier rigid bodies own their own transform. Never mirror physics position into React
  state — read it through a ref (`rigidBody.current.translation()`).
- Drive bodies with `applyImpulse`, `setLinvel`, `setNextKinematicTranslation`. Do not
  set `position` props on a body to move it.
- Collision and intersection handlers (`onCollisionEnter`, `onIntersectionEnter`) are the
  event path; per-frame polling is the fallback path. Keep the two from double-firing.

## State

All shared game state lives in `src/stores/gameStore.ts`. Subscribe with selectors
(`useGameStore(s => s.phase)`), never destructure the whole store, or every component
re-renders on every change. Phase transitions go through the store's action functions —
do not `set` phase fields from a component.

## Composition and style

Components are declarative JSX plus refs for imperative work. Delegate real logic to a
hook or a `systems/` function rather than growing a component. Explicit return types on
exports (`(): React.ReactElement`). No CSS framework — `ui/` uses inline style objects
in the black / ice-cyan `#1ad9e8` / amber-orange `#f06e14` neon palette. No semicolons, single
quotes, 2-space indent, relative imports only.
